---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import { TEKST } from "../../config";

const titel = "A customer requires ISO 27001 or a security questionnaire";
const beschrijving =
  "A customer asks for ISO 27001 or a security questionnaire. What is usually missing, and what a gap scan delivers. No certificate and no accountant's report.";
---

<Base titel={titel} beschrijving={beschrijving} taal="en" lees>
  <h1>{titel}</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    A customer asks for ISO 27001, or a customer asks for a security
    questionnaire, and there is a date under it.
  </p>

  <h2>The situation</h2>
  <p>
    The demand comes from an enterprise customer or from a tender. It is about
    ISO 27001 for a SaaS firm, an IT provider or an MSP, or about completing a
    security questionnaire.
  </p>

  <h2>What is usually missing</h2>
  <p>
    The policy, the risk register and the evidence do not meet. The
    questionnaire is empty, or the answers cannot be traced to a document that
    is still true.
  </p>

  <h2>What the scan delivers</h2>
  <p>
    A gap register and advice on the next step. If the trigger is a security
    questionnaire, that includes a prepared or completed list, as far as the
    documents allow.
  </p>

  <h2>Limits</h2>
  <p>
    I do not issue a certificate. Accredited certification bodies do that. I
    do not judge the statute. I do not issue an accountant's report. The
    person who implements does not do the independent internal audit (not a
    certification audit) for the same client. I never certify my own work.
  </p>

  <h2>In short</h2>
  <p>
    How long it takes depends on what already exists and on the deadline. That
    is not fixed until the intake. You supply the demand in the customer's
    words, the date, and what can be reused.
  </p>
  <p>
    Implementation and an independent internal audit are two next steps, not
    the same person for the same client.
  </p>

  <p><a class="knop" href="/en/contact/">{TEKST.en.cta}</a></p>
</Base>
